WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.064 --> 00:00:07.846
There is a world where nature still hides some of her most beautiful secrets.

00:00:09.805 --> 00:00:12.606
A notch in the earth's crust between Africa,

00:00:13.227 --> 00:00:14.247
Asia and Europe.

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:17.368
The Mediterranean.

00:00:18.509 --> 00:00:27.252
15,000 islands surrounded by crystal clear water.

00:00:31.533 --> 00:00:34.795
A deep sea where extraordinary wildlife reigns.

00:00:45.283 --> 00:00:49.045
So blue they attract visitors from all over the world.

00:00:52.548 --> 00:00:55.471
This sea has witnessed the birth of civilizations.

00:00:57.816 --> 00:00:58.716
The first cities.

00:01:00.697 --> 00:01:02.018
The first seafarers.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:11.481
No natural space has been so affected by the presence of mankind.

00:01:17.864 --> 00:01:19.105
How do they adapt to us?

00:01:20.704 --> 00:01:23.105
How do they succeed in giving birth?

00:01:24.087 --> 00:01:24.867
Raising their young?

00:01:25.927 --> 00:01:26.487
Growing up?

00:01:28.644 --> 00:01:29.703
Finding a mate.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:34.126
Pushing beyond the limits.

00:01:37.768 --> 00:01:39.287
Conquering new territories.

00:01:47.731 --> 00:01:49.352
Under attack on all fronts.

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:53.814
How can this remarkable sea withstand this pressure?

00:01:55.555 --> 00:01:56.756
Can she heal her wounds?

00:01:59.908 --> 00:02:00.987
Can she regenerate?

00:02:11.353 --> 00:02:16.474
These are the incredible stories of the living beings in the Mediterranean today.

00:02:29.863 --> 00:02:30.643
It's September.

00:02:32.704 --> 00:02:34.125
On the south coast of France,

00:02:34.865 --> 00:02:36.945
a great traveler is making her way.

00:02:44.868 --> 00:02:46.288
She's a loggerhead turtle.

00:02:48.009 --> 00:02:49.909
In the great family of sea turtles,

00:02:50.409 --> 00:02:53.010
the loggerhead is the most Mediterranean of them all.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:03:02.265
This young female is 25 years old and is suddenly undergoing a transformation.

00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:03.906
Inside her body,

00:03:04.647 --> 00:03:06.829
a biological clock has just gone off.

00:03:16.497 --> 00:03:18.359
From the other end of the Mediterranean,

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:22.182
a powerful urge calls to her for the very first time.

00:03:24.439 --> 00:03:25.721
Turtle heads south.

00:03:27.322 --> 00:03:29.844
She is leaving the French coast for the open sea.

00:03:32.347 --> 00:03:34.489
She must return to the place she was born.

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:40.493
Crossing almost the entire Mediterranean.

00:03:41.433 --> 00:03:43.555
An odyssey of 4,000 kilometers.

00:03:44.576 --> 00:03:46.217
Her destination is Kiparissia,

00:03:46.299 --> 00:03:47.239
a beach in Greece.

00:03:57.592 --> 00:04:00.234
Six exhausting months through perilous waters.

00:04:10.741 --> 00:04:11.181
Goes well?

00:04:11.902 --> 00:04:15.965
She will be there just in time for the most important task of her life.

00:04:18.026 --> 00:04:18.665
Giving birth.

00:04:31.706 --> 00:04:35.108
But how can she find this place 25 years after leaving it?

00:04:37.229 --> 00:04:38.010
To navigate,

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:41.372
Turtle uses all her sensory abilities.

00:04:43.433 --> 00:04:49.177
Her powerful sense of smell allows her to analyze the sense of the currents and the coastlines.

00:04:52.516 --> 00:04:53.538
Thanks to her taste,

00:04:53.898 --> 00:04:57.845
she has memorized the different types of water in each place she has been through.

00:05:02.579 --> 00:05:04.460
She has another incredible ability,

00:05:05.781 --> 00:05:08.801
an acute sense of the Earth's magnetic field.

00:05:12.762 --> 00:05:14.382
As if equipped with GPS,

00:05:14.863 --> 00:05:18.964
she knows her precise location on the planet at any given moment.

00:05:22.065 --> 00:05:27.966
This sensory toolkit allows her to remember all the places she has been in her entire life,

00:05:28.687 --> 00:05:29.487
as if on a map.

00:05:31.452 --> 00:05:34.573
She can set her course towards whichever place she chooses,

00:05:35.033 --> 00:05:35.973
just from her memory.

00:05:39.314 --> 00:05:39.694
And yet,

00:05:40.355 --> 00:05:42.855
she isn't connected to any satellite.

00:05:50.698 --> 00:05:53.939
South of the Mediterranean is the largest desert in the world.

00:05:55.699 --> 00:05:56.439
The Sahara.

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:05.430
Thousands of white storks are traveling through.

00:06:07.451 --> 00:06:08.893
Having spent the winter in Mali,

00:06:09.393 --> 00:06:11.334
they are returning to Europe for the summer.

00:06:14.336 --> 00:06:16.617
A dangerous journey they make every year.

00:06:22.242 --> 00:06:23.343
But for this young male,

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:24.923
it's the first time.

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:27.805
He follows his elders.

00:06:28.346 --> 00:06:28.987
They know the way.

00:06:36.372 --> 00:06:40.058
A male is still single and only has one thing in mind.

00:06:42.324 --> 00:06:43.445
Meeting a female.

00:06:52.896 --> 00:06:55.858
Most migratory birds travel at night in the cooler,

00:06:55.937 --> 00:06:56.998
calmer conditions.

00:06:57.879 --> 00:06:58.279
Storks,

00:06:58.319 --> 00:06:58.699
however,

00:06:59.120 --> 00:07:00.361
only travel during the day.

00:07:01.302 --> 00:07:03.543
For the large bodies to glide through the skies,

00:07:03.884 --> 00:07:05.945
they need the help of a natural elevator.

00:07:06.526 --> 00:07:07.067
Hot air.

00:07:30.935 --> 00:07:33.357
After 5,000 kilometers of sand dunes,

00:07:33.716 --> 00:07:35.637
there is now a new obstacle to cross.

00:07:38.178 --> 00:07:38.600
The sea,

00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:44.502
the Mediterranean and the famous Strait of Gibraltar.

00:07:47.685 --> 00:07:47.985
Here,

00:07:48.264 --> 00:07:49.245
in the north of Morocco,

00:07:49.786 --> 00:07:52.726
is the shortest crossing between Africa and Europe.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.482
14 kilometers to reach Spain.

00:08:00.704 --> 00:08:03.086
The young male doesn't know how to tackle it.

00:08:04.487 --> 00:08:06.149
You can't fly over water.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:08.230
There's no lift.

00:08:08.511 --> 00:08:09.812
The air isn't heated.

00:08:11.173 --> 00:08:12.334
If he touches the water,

00:08:12.853 --> 00:08:13.875
it's certain death.

00:08:16.757 --> 00:08:19.359
So he waits for the others to show him the way.

00:08:23.552 --> 00:08:26.194
Stalks travel across continents to find a mate,

00:08:28.235 --> 00:08:30.197
while others cross the ocean.

00:08:32.057 --> 00:08:33.399
The middle of the Atlantic.

00:08:36.081 --> 00:08:38.722
Bluefin tuna are arriving from all over the ocean.

00:08:40.485 --> 00:08:44.047
They gather in their thousands and all set off for the same destination.

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:56.247
the mediterranean an army of 3 000 in peak condition colossal fish measuring up to 3 meters and over 600 kilograms

00:09:01.110 --> 00:09:03.754
They cut through the water at 70 kilometers an hour.

00:09:07.899 --> 00:09:09.461
They speed on day and night,

00:09:09.861 --> 00:09:10.763
even while they sleep.

00:09:10.783 --> 00:09:11.644
They're fast.

00:09:38.964 --> 00:09:42.026
It's the last meal before the most decisive moment of their lives.

00:09:47.511 --> 00:09:48.271
Here we go again,

00:09:48.951 --> 00:09:51.073
all together towards the promised land.

00:09:53.275 --> 00:09:54.696
But why the Mediterranean?

00:09:55.597 --> 00:09:57.158
They must breed where they were born.

00:09:58.139 --> 00:10:00.000
So it has been since the dawn of time.

00:10:04.509 --> 00:10:08.913
They will make a journey of thousands of kilometers towards their final destination,

00:10:09.694 --> 00:10:11.016
the Balearic Islands.

00:10:11.737 --> 00:10:15.581
The first dangerous stage is to pass through the gateway to the Mediterranean,

00:10:17.162 --> 00:10:18.403
the Strait of Gibraltar.

00:10:28.465 --> 00:10:29.546
On the Moroccan coast,

00:10:29.826 --> 00:10:33.469
the young stork is waiting for a signal from the more experienced adults.

00:10:37.032 --> 00:10:37.872
They are taking off.

00:10:39.113 --> 00:10:40.234
It's time for him to go.

00:10:50.902 --> 00:10:52.744
The warm air rises from the ground.

00:10:54.464 --> 00:10:56.785
It lifts him higher as he turns.

00:11:00.807 --> 00:11:02.067
A thermal elevator.

00:11:10.393 --> 00:11:12.014
His wings span two meters.

00:11:12.614 --> 00:11:17.336
The feathers at their tips spread out like fingers and feel the invisible thermals.

00:11:18.998 --> 00:11:20.479
They guide him in the wind.

00:11:29.745 --> 00:11:32.829
The plan is to rise as high as possible above the coast.

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:36.091
Up to 1,000 meters.

00:11:40.815 --> 00:11:42.016
They are high enough now.

00:11:43.557 --> 00:11:44.899
Their crossing can begin.

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:49.702
They glide to the other shore.

00:11:53.206 --> 00:11:55.047
The great descent towards Spain.

00:12:03.212 --> 00:12:16.101
this feat can only be pulled off in certain conditions strong sunshine with no wind some

00:12:16.142 --> 00:12:17.962
have been waiting for weeks to cross

00:12:25.135 --> 00:12:27.817
The young male senses his altitude dropping dangerously.

00:12:44.049 --> 00:12:44.389
Land,

00:12:44.831 --> 00:12:45.390
at last,

00:12:49.213 --> 00:12:49.894
he made it.

00:12:54.903 --> 00:12:56.326
First stop for all travelers,

00:12:57.507 --> 00:12:59.008
Donana National Park.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:02.292
The largest wetland in Spain,

00:13:02.772 --> 00:13:05.435
irrigated by the estuary of the Guadalquivir River.

00:13:08.639 --> 00:13:11.942
Food here is plentiful and so are potential mates.

00:13:24.951 --> 00:13:28.236
The young male can now move on to his most important project.

00:13:29.817 --> 00:13:30.677
Meeting a female,

00:13:31.139 --> 00:13:31.920
forming a couple,

00:13:32.581 --> 00:13:33.341
having chicks.

00:13:35.824 --> 00:13:36.665
But for storks,

00:13:37.086 --> 00:13:40.409
there is one condition for getting any female's attention.

00:13:43.873 --> 00:13:45.135
You must have a nest.

00:13:48.239 --> 00:13:50.861
Knowing that a presentable nest takes years to make,

00:13:51.301 --> 00:13:53.782
the young male is looking for a second hand one.

00:14:02.427 --> 00:14:02.808
That one?

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:05.909
Nope,

00:14:06.290 --> 00:14:06.971
already taken.

00:14:10.032 --> 00:14:12.273
How about this one?

00:14:13.174 --> 00:14:14.014
That one's taken too.

00:14:16.351 --> 00:14:18.772
They are all occupied and well guarded.

00:14:22.333 --> 00:14:23.053
In this area,

00:14:23.774 --> 00:14:25.834
there aren't any free spaces left.

00:14:32.015 --> 00:14:33.317
A few kilometers away,

00:14:33.876 --> 00:14:34.976
in the middle of the strait,

00:14:35.756 --> 00:14:37.997
the 3,000 tuna are crossing the pass.

00:14:47.288 --> 00:14:48.954
They split into two groups.

00:14:50.159 --> 00:14:52.708
The northern group chooses to follow the coastline.

00:15:01.553 --> 00:15:04.337
But there is an unexpected obstacle in their path.

00:15:27.524 --> 00:15:32.508
The second group is heading through the middle of the strait where the sentries posted.

00:15:36.771 --> 00:15:38.292
A family of orcas.

00:15:40.673 --> 00:15:41.774
They will take their share.

00:17:10.168 --> 00:17:11.469
300 tuna less.

00:17:13.269 --> 00:17:14.609
They won't have any offspring.

00:17:20.992 --> 00:17:22.873
The middle group is still en route.

00:17:23.533 --> 00:17:25.615
Most of the troops were able to pass through.

00:17:26.514 --> 00:17:28.855
Now they head for the Balearic Islands.

00:17:35.288 --> 00:17:37.609
The young male still hasn't found a free nest.

00:17:38.390 --> 00:17:40.131
His exploration leads him north.

00:17:42.552 --> 00:17:45.334
After Andalusia is the region of Extremadura,

00:17:46.894 --> 00:17:49.135
the lookout point of Los Barrecos.

00:17:56.299 --> 00:17:59.001
Perched on top are several very old nests,

00:17:59.362 --> 00:18:00.722
but even those are occupied.

00:18:12.688 --> 00:18:13.228
Trujillo,

00:18:13.749 --> 00:18:15.850
a pretty calm little town.

00:18:21.014 --> 00:18:22.935
Will there be any available spots here?

00:18:27.298 --> 00:18:27.959
How about here?

00:18:31.642 --> 00:18:32.842
The neighbours seem nice.

00:18:37.346 --> 00:18:37.586
Oh no,

00:18:38.066 --> 00:18:39.507
this rotten old nest won't do.

00:18:46.295 --> 00:18:49.136
The young male has finally found a smart little nest.

00:18:50.037 --> 00:18:50.857
Unfortunately,

00:18:51.377 --> 00:18:52.778
the weather vane is in the way.

00:18:59.821 --> 00:19:00.301
No matter,

00:19:00.701 --> 00:19:02.222
this nest is fantastic.

00:19:02.922 --> 00:19:04.523
Surely the females will love it.

00:19:08.745 --> 00:19:09.285
He waits.

00:19:11.286 --> 00:19:12.007
Days go by.

00:19:14.335 --> 00:19:15.455
No females show up.

00:19:19.637 --> 00:19:20.577
Is it the weather vane?

00:19:21.357 --> 00:19:22.678
Or is the town too quiet?

00:19:24.398 --> 00:19:25.538
Everyone here is old.

00:19:31.960 --> 00:19:33.901
After a week without a single visit,

00:19:34.561 --> 00:19:36.302
the young male decides to move.

00:19:56.324 --> 00:19:58.859
Special structures have been built here for storks.

00:20:04.876 --> 00:20:07.457
The young male attempts to take a nest by force.

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:24.470
But

00:20:24.471 --> 00:20:26.732
he is much too young to challenge the grown-ups.

00:20:32.096 --> 00:20:32.857
What about that one?

00:20:34.599 --> 00:20:35.759
Don't even think about it.

00:20:41.465 --> 00:20:44.328
Growing up and making your way in life is never easy.

00:20:45.209 --> 00:20:47.031
You must fight and not lose hope.

00:20:50.913 --> 00:20:51.575
Keep trying,

00:20:52.055 --> 00:20:53.036
again and again.

00:20:58.911 --> 00:20:59.472
On his way,

00:20:59.932 --> 00:21:02.074
he finds an unexpected food source.

00:21:10.303 --> 00:21:11.384
It won't make him sick.

00:21:11.985 --> 00:21:15.729
A stork's stomach is so resistant it can digest almost anything.

00:21:27.031 --> 00:21:30.853
This landfill site has become a daily buffet for a group of storks.

00:21:31.733 --> 00:21:33.713
They completely change their way of life.

00:21:35.355 --> 00:21:39.557
They have food all year round and no longer make the great voyage to Africa.

00:21:40.356 --> 00:21:41.216
They have settled.

00:21:45.338 --> 00:21:46.378
The world is changing.

00:21:47.199 --> 00:21:48.099
So are the storks.

00:21:53.591 --> 00:21:55.813
The young male has other concerns right now.

00:21:57.294 --> 00:21:58.775
Has he learned from his failures?

00:21:59.976 --> 00:22:01.877
He has lowered his ambitions somewhat.

00:22:03.539 --> 00:22:05.201
He is ready to start from scratch,

00:22:06.121 --> 00:22:06.781
find a spot,

00:22:07.602 --> 00:22:09.223
and build his own nest himself.

00:22:21.171 --> 00:22:25.115
After swimming for 10 days and covering 350 kilometers,

00:22:25.855 --> 00:22:28.136
Turtle is making her first stop,

00:22:28.976 --> 00:22:29.477
Corsica.

00:22:40.105 --> 00:22:41.285
She is at the coast again,

00:22:41.965 --> 00:22:43.106
where she can find food.

00:23:00.243 --> 00:23:06.265
She loves the sponges she dislodges from the rocks and the shellfish that she can smell beneath the sand.

00:23:24.851 --> 00:23:25.452
After lunch,

00:23:26.693 --> 00:23:28.475
a little siesta in the sunshine,

00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:35.702
bringing her body temperature back up to the right level.

00:24:02.647 --> 00:24:08.691
Turtle leaves Corsica and turns towards the Italian coast and the lagoon current that will carry her south.

00:24:19.095 --> 00:24:20.096
In the Mediterranean,

00:24:20.715 --> 00:24:22.896
turtles face no dangers from nature.

00:24:25.317 --> 00:24:25.498
Well,

00:24:26.658 --> 00:24:27.239
almost none.

00:24:32.119 --> 00:24:32.859
Her weak point,

00:24:33.319 --> 00:24:35.400
the most vulnerable part of her armor,

00:24:36.820 --> 00:24:37.621
is her stomach.

00:24:53.745 --> 00:24:54.166
Normally

00:24:54.646 --> 00:24:55.586
sharks won't dare.

00:25:17.331 --> 00:25:20.713
There is another danger that Turtle has learned to overcome.

00:25:25.016 --> 00:25:26.236
It looks like a jellyfish,

00:25:26.476 --> 00:25:26.997
but isn't.

00:25:30.098 --> 00:25:31.059
They are not for eating.

00:25:31.439 --> 00:25:33.100
She has known that for a long time.

00:25:34.981 --> 00:25:35.681
In the past,

00:25:36.102 --> 00:25:38.843
she only encountered them here and there along the coast.

00:25:39.484 --> 00:25:40.125
But recently,

00:25:40.544 --> 00:25:42.125
they have appeared in large shoals.

00:25:46.807 --> 00:25:49.969
A plastic vortex in the open sea.

00:25:54.950 --> 00:25:59.971
The equivalent of 34,000 plastic bottles ends up in the Mediterranean every minute.

00:26:01.951 --> 00:26:03.011
Turtle doesn't know it.

00:26:04.353 --> 00:26:05.053
She's living it.

00:26:08.394 --> 00:26:11.795
While she may know the difference between a plastic bag and a jellyfish,

00:26:13.355 --> 00:26:15.016
others sometimes get it wrong.

00:26:18.539 --> 00:26:27.663
This young male has already swallowed too much plastic and now he has gas in his intestines.

00:26:28.244 --> 00:26:29.504
He can no longer dive.

00:26:32.444 --> 00:26:34.385
He bobs on the surface like a cork.

00:26:50.751 --> 00:26:51.813
There's nothing she can do.

00:26:56.336 --> 00:26:57.817
He won't get out of this one.

00:27:07.023 --> 00:27:08.183
Nothing stops Turtle.

00:27:08.703 --> 00:27:11.425
She's possessed by an overpowering urge,

00:27:12.586 --> 00:27:13.847
the desire to breed.

00:27:20.412 --> 00:27:22.692
The tuna have reached their final destination,

00:27:23.653 --> 00:27:25.313
the Balearic Archipelago.

00:27:27.794 --> 00:27:29.334
Beautiful sheltered bays,

00:27:30.275 --> 00:27:31.255
perfect temperature.

00:27:33.235 --> 00:27:35.296
It's paradise for the bluefin tuna.

00:27:41.557 --> 00:27:44.258
Here they will carry out their greatest mission.

00:27:50.019 --> 00:27:53.462
Waiting for the full moon and their night of fertility.

00:27:59.690 --> 00:28:00.891
This is the moment.

00:28:01.991 --> 00:28:03.754
The big night for bluefin tuna.

00:28:06.836 --> 00:28:08.418
There is excitement in the water.

00:28:11.115 --> 00:28:13.378
The females have swollen bellies full of eggs.

00:28:16.139 --> 00:28:17.801
They release tens of millions.

00:28:21.263 --> 00:28:23.484
The males fertilize those eggs with their semen.

00:28:26.285 --> 00:28:28.566
They beat their tails to mix everything together.

00:28:33.307 --> 00:28:35.527
An eternal ballet creating life.

00:28:43.109 --> 00:28:45.469
They will hatch hundreds of billions of larvae.

00:29:01.535 --> 00:29:03.298
This is the bluefin tuna's home.

00:29:04.538 --> 00:29:06.339
They have no natural predator here.

00:29:11.464 --> 00:29:14.627
But a formidable enemy is watching them very closely.

00:29:20.532 --> 00:29:24.817
An armada of boats follows their every movement with powerful sonars.

00:29:56.567 --> 00:29:59.798
These lords of the sea are transferred to fish farms.

00:30:03.907 --> 00:30:06.990
They are fed before becoming food themselves.

00:30:13.076 --> 00:30:15.519
3,000 of them entered the Mediterranean.

00:30:16.659 --> 00:30:16.879
Now,

00:30:17.260 --> 00:30:18.461
there are only 300.

00:30:20.763 --> 00:30:23.567
These few escapees have avoided all the traps.

00:30:25.268 --> 00:30:28.330
But they were able to mate and produce the next generation.

00:30:33.992 --> 00:30:38.234
All that is left for them to do is pass through the Strait of Gibraltar once more,

00:30:39.054 --> 00:30:40.075
back to the Atlantic.

00:30:43.896 --> 00:30:45.137
Because of overfishing,

00:30:45.697 --> 00:30:48.758
bluefin tuna almost disappeared from the Mediterranean in the

00:30:49.478 --> 00:30:49.598
2000s.

00:30:50.499 --> 00:30:52.119
But the situation is improving.

00:30:53.640 --> 00:30:55.401
Thanks to quotas that limit catches,

00:30:55.921 --> 00:30:57.882
they have been able to reproduce abundantly.

00:30:59.102 --> 00:31:01.323
We have avoided the collapse of their population,

00:31:02.663 --> 00:31:03.024
for now.

00:31:06.487 --> 00:31:10.210
The young male is now looking for a modest site to build his nest.

00:31:14.153 --> 00:31:16.195
He has found a work of art he likes.

00:31:19.057 --> 00:31:19.938
The top is taken.

00:31:20.918 --> 00:31:21.999
The higher floors too.

00:31:23.500 --> 00:31:25.042
But the mezzanine looks vacant.

00:31:29.905 --> 00:31:30.366
It's bare,

00:31:30.506 --> 00:31:31.867
but at least it's available.

00:31:34.980 --> 00:31:36.481
The dorm is on the second floor.

00:31:39.225 --> 00:31:39.825
On the third,

00:31:40.226 --> 00:31:41.968
a studio for amorous stopovers.

00:31:44.711 --> 00:31:47.234
The penthouse has a stunning view but it's too windy.

00:31:49.596 --> 00:31:51.298
Medicine isn't so bad after all.

00:32:01.836 --> 00:32:05.138
There is still a lot of work to do to make the nest worthy of its name.

00:32:06.819 --> 00:32:07.660
But all of a sudden,

00:32:08.600 --> 00:32:10.081
the young male has a visitor.

00:32:18.666 --> 00:32:20.367
A little customary clattering.

00:32:21.188 --> 00:32:22.028
If she responds,

00:32:22.608 --> 00:32:23.749
that is a good first step.

00:32:37.399 --> 00:32:37.659
Success.

00:32:38.580 --> 00:32:39.241
She's interested.

00:32:42.525 --> 00:32:44.086
The young male insists,

00:32:44.087 --> 00:32:44.467
checking,

00:32:45.208 --> 00:32:45.928
making sure,

00:32:46.629 --> 00:32:47.451
sealing the bond.

00:33:05.548 --> 00:33:07.689
The next step is hers to take.

00:33:19.012 --> 00:33:19.772
In that moment,

00:33:20.112 --> 00:33:22.952
the young male knows he has reached the end of his voyage.

00:33:23.913 --> 00:33:27.534
His project has succeeded after so many missteps.

00:33:28.775 --> 00:33:32.836
He can hope to couple up and be sitting on some eggs within a fortnight.

00:33:35.531 --> 00:33:42.135
They will learn to live together and in a few years they will have the most beautiful nest in Extremadura.

00:34:00.945 --> 00:34:01.446
Turtle

00:34:01.527 --> 00:34:03.127
has been traveling for three weeks.

00:34:04.311 --> 00:34:05.491
She's now heading south.

00:34:08.512 --> 00:34:10.213
She has reached the Italian coast.

00:34:15.895 --> 00:34:16.135
Here,

00:34:16.416 --> 00:34:18.677
the mountains plunge steeply into the sea.

00:34:22.757 --> 00:34:26.079
One of the problems of this coast is that there is nothing to eat.

00:34:26.739 --> 00:34:28.619
The strip of coastline is too narrow.

00:34:32.056 --> 00:34:35.860
Turtle knows she can try her luck in these places where humans live.

00:34:39.722 --> 00:34:42.264
The ports are stocked with untapped riches.

00:35:03.829 --> 00:35:07.413
A turtle doesn't know she has entered someone else's territory.

00:35:09.094 --> 00:35:11.335
A huge male jealously guarding his goods.

00:35:57.847 --> 00:35:59.990
Fishermen are not the turtles enemies,

00:36:01.072 --> 00:36:03.494
but their equipment claims many victims.

00:36:08.159 --> 00:36:10.262
The most dangerous are the ghost nets.

00:36:11.503 --> 00:36:14.186
These unowned traps can drift for many years.

00:36:51.062 --> 00:36:51.302
Thanks

00:36:51.322 --> 00:36:52.042
to the currents,

00:36:52.461 --> 00:36:55.223
Turtle has made quick progress along the Italian coast.

00:36:55.723 --> 00:36:57.684
She now makes a remarkable decision.

00:37:00.496 --> 00:37:02.237
Instead of navigating around Sicily,

00:37:02.617 --> 00:37:03.358
she heads south,

00:37:03.778 --> 00:37:05.579
directly towards the Strait of Messina.

00:37:07.942 --> 00:37:10.483
How does she know that by taking this corridor,

00:37:10.945 --> 00:37:13.246
she's saving herself hundreds of kilometers?

00:37:29.851 --> 00:37:31.472
This strait is incredibly dangerous.

00:37:31.992 --> 00:37:33.473
Intense maritime traffic,

00:37:34.094 --> 00:37:35.634
fishing boats in the hundreds.

00:37:49.202 --> 00:37:53.924
The cold waters in this deep strait are very rich in plankton and

00:37:54.004 --> 00:37:56.106
also in prey for turtles.

00:38:02.025 --> 00:38:02.925
Her favorite meal.

00:38:14.389 --> 00:38:18.152
Turtles play an important role in controlling the population of jellyfish.

00:38:24.514 --> 00:38:25.755
After the Strait of Messina,

00:38:25.835 --> 00:38:26.695
she turns east.

00:38:40.935 --> 00:38:41.536
It's March.

00:38:41.956 --> 00:38:44.717
She has already traveled 3,000 kilometers.

00:38:48.759 --> 00:38:49.958
She is not the only one.

00:38:55.226 --> 00:38:56.887
The mating season has begun.

00:39:02.512 --> 00:39:05.576
Hundreds and thousands of them come here every year.

00:39:13.503 --> 00:39:17.746
Turtle has come to the end of her journey after six months of migration.

00:39:39.639 --> 00:39:43.864
The rise in temperature and daylight are waking their reproductive instincts.

00:39:45.407 --> 00:39:47.068
The males have gathered near the shore.

00:39:47.590 --> 00:39:49.692
The females are arriving from the sea.

00:39:50.913 --> 00:39:51.134
Now,

00:39:51.534 --> 00:39:52.815
it's time to meet a partner.

00:40:09.645 --> 00:40:11.727
There are lots of males that want to mate with her.

00:40:13.788 --> 00:40:14.649
Turtle approves.

00:40:18.231 --> 00:40:21.654
She is able to fertilize her eggs with several partners sperm.

00:40:24.596 --> 00:40:27.498
She will have babies with many different biological fathers.

00:40:29.824 --> 00:40:32.066
and a higher probability of strong lineage.

00:40:32.766 --> 00:40:33.347
Pretty clever.

00:40:41.673 --> 00:40:42.774
In the natural world,

00:40:43.234 --> 00:40:44.955
it's normally the mother that gives birth.

00:40:46.797 --> 00:40:48.597
Except in one unusual family,

00:40:49.278 --> 00:40:50.539
who takes a different approach.

00:40:53.762 --> 00:40:55.983
Have the father bear the offspring.

00:41:03.711 --> 00:41:07.695
This is the strange story of the male seahorse's pregnancy.

00:41:14.539 --> 00:41:17.081
Seahorse is a fish with the head of a horse.

00:41:20.643 --> 00:41:27.887
He has two little dorsal fins that propel him forwards and two others behind his head to adjust his course.

00:41:30.369 --> 00:41:31.811
A mouth with no teeth?

00:41:35.793 --> 00:41:36.954
to gulp down shrimp,

00:41:42.679 --> 00:41:43.440
but not the shells.

00:41:49.164 --> 00:41:49.505
Today,

00:41:50.025 --> 00:41:51.686
Seahorse isn't looking for food.

00:41:54.869 --> 00:41:56.632
He has a romantic rendezvous.

00:42:05.579 --> 00:42:08.463
A private meeting with absolute discretion.

00:42:26.818 --> 00:42:27.119
After

00:42:27.119 --> 00:42:28.581
a few intimate exchanges,

00:42:29.221 --> 00:42:31.664
she lays her eggs in the male's belly.

00:42:41.804 --> 00:42:44.525
This romance takes place in the Tau Lagoon,

00:42:45.086 --> 00:42:47.807
a small sheltered inland sea in southern France.

00:42:52.630 --> 00:42:55.891
Men have farmed shellfish on ropes here for the last hundred years.

00:42:58.313 --> 00:43:00.254
Seahorses take advantage of the calm,

00:43:00.754 --> 00:43:01.034
warm,

00:43:01.234 --> 00:43:02.835
shallow waters to breed here.

00:43:13.324 --> 00:43:14.704
Seahorse is pregnant.

00:43:17.126 --> 00:43:21.567
He's gotten really big with all the discomfort and irritation that brings.

00:43:25.028 --> 00:43:27.090
Two weeks have passed since they mated.

00:43:39.815 --> 00:43:41.076
He's going into labor.

00:43:43.115 --> 00:43:44.137
First contractions.

00:43:50.682 --> 00:43:51.963
Push.

00:44:00.251 --> 00:44:01.932
Push.

00:44:01.952 --> 00:44:03.295
He's giving birth.

00:44:23.466 --> 00:44:24.467
A mother-father.

00:44:25.568 --> 00:44:28.010
It's one of nature's most remarkable oddities.

00:44:32.595 --> 00:44:34.677
The babies will begin their lives alone,

00:44:35.597 --> 00:44:36.499
without their parents'

00:44:36.539 --> 00:44:36.759
help.

00:44:46.179 --> 00:44:48.362
The father won't have time to rest.

00:44:49.625 --> 00:44:52.648
Mother has another batch ready and is eager to go again.

00:44:56.534 --> 00:44:59.699
He will be continuously pregnant until the end of summer.

00:45:05.731 --> 00:45:08.112
Turtle is now ready for the final challenge.

00:45:09.052 --> 00:45:10.454
She has reached Kiparisia,

00:45:11.034 --> 00:45:13.215
the place where she was born 25 years ago.

00:45:23.498 --> 00:45:24.860
Scenery has changed a bit.

00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:27.221
She needs to go a little further.

00:45:45.759 --> 00:45:48.802
Turtle has to haul herself out of her normal environment.

00:45:58.510 --> 00:46:02.874
She strains to drag her 150 kilograms across the sand.

00:46:06.215 --> 00:46:06.757
On land,

00:46:07.456 --> 00:46:07.978
it's hell.

00:46:12.302 --> 00:46:14.664
Not to mention all the egg thieves on the brawl.

00:46:24.032 --> 00:46:26.594
Why machine flick this punishment on herself?

00:46:29.476 --> 00:46:31.719
It's a legacy of the distant past.

00:46:34.067 --> 00:46:36.089
When her ancestors lived on the land,

00:46:37.630 --> 00:46:41.192
she digs into the sand to bury her eggs as deep as she can.

00:46:49.678 --> 00:46:52.620
Hiding her treasure so no one can find it.

00:47:04.703 --> 00:47:06.904
They can always see where she lays her eggs.

00:47:11.786 --> 00:47:13.427
But she has a trick for the thieves.

00:47:35.974 --> 00:47:40.838
She leaves around a hundred eggs in the sand that will hatch in 50 days.

00:47:48.123 --> 00:47:49.826
She's finished her task as a mother.

00:47:55.150 --> 00:48:00.333
Turtle has actually laid her eggs three meters away from the place where she dug her hole.

00:48:04.743 --> 00:48:06.644
The dogs can search all they like.

00:48:18.167 --> 00:48:21.508
Turtles haven't changed their nesting sites for millions of years.

00:48:24.709 --> 00:48:25.069
Today,

00:48:25.629 --> 00:48:31.351
these places are beaches prized by huge numbers of tourists who pose a threat to the survival of the eggs.

00:48:52.514 --> 00:48:52.754
Some

00:48:52.835 --> 00:48:57.078
men and women have woken up to the fragility of the turtle's existence.

00:49:00.407 --> 00:49:03.889
These young volunteers come in their hundreds from all over Europe.

00:49:16.418 --> 00:49:21.961
They are here with an organization that has been successfully protecting turtles for the last 30 years.

00:49:26.440 --> 00:49:27.701
Across the Mediterranean,

00:49:28.260 --> 00:49:31.423
the number of nesting sites has significantly increased.

00:49:32.883 --> 00:49:33.844
That's great news.

00:49:38.967 --> 00:49:42.307
Turtle leaves behind hundreds of future lives.

00:49:43.609 --> 00:49:48.510
She's betting on the fact that at least some of them will survive to carry on the species.

00:49:50.092 --> 00:49:50.713
And it works.

00:49:51.793 --> 00:49:56.037
Turtles have withstood every disaster since the age of the dinosaurs.

00:49:57.557 --> 00:49:59.359
They are still here.

00:50:00.119 --> 00:50:01.020
Yes,

00:50:01.021 --> 00:50:09.568
my Parents in the Mediterranean have undertaken incredible efforts to give birth

00:50:13.632 --> 00:50:19.036
Under the sand in the nest and in the currents new life is being born everywhere

00:50:23.780 --> 00:50:25.702
What will become of all these little ones

00:50:29.559 --> 00:50:32.121
How can they thrive in this Mediterranean world?

00:50:49.090 --> 00:50:49.331
He's

00:50:49.351 --> 00:50:51.211
an eight-month-old finwell calf,

00:50:52.052 --> 00:50:55.034
a big baby weighing eight tons and ten meters long.

00:50:59.384 --> 00:51:00.744
The time has come to grow up,

00:51:01.345 --> 00:51:02.286
to make his own way,

00:51:02.807 --> 00:51:04.608
to feed himself by his own means.

00:51:08.329 --> 00:51:10.192
Except he doesn't know how to find food.

00:51:11.633 --> 00:51:12.874
He still needs his mother.

00:51:24.327 --> 00:51:24.968
Until now,

00:51:25.548 --> 00:51:27.990
all he's had to do is come to her belly and suckle.

00:51:29.010 --> 00:51:31.652
70 litres of milk flowed into his mouth.

00:51:34.052 --> 00:51:34.574
It's all gone.

00:51:35.314 --> 00:51:36.615
His mother is still there,

00:51:37.115 --> 00:51:38.256
but the milk has dried up.

00:51:44.228 --> 00:51:45.469
Four tons of fish a day.

00:51:46.190 --> 00:51:48.311
That's a normal diet for a world like him.

00:51:51.394 --> 00:51:52.494
You will have to learn.

00:51:53.776 --> 00:51:54.195
But how?

00:52:00.760 --> 00:52:03.784
His mother has just located a sardine shore down below.

00:52:10.829 --> 00:52:12.490
She leaves her calf on his own.

00:52:14.617 --> 00:52:15.617
He can't follow her.

00:52:18.800 --> 00:52:21.461
Little Finn is not yet able to dive to great depths.

00:52:23.984 --> 00:52:26.086
But he can still communicate with her through song.

00:52:30.548 --> 00:52:32.791
Mother and baby send signals to each other.

00:52:34.172 --> 00:52:38.635
This allows them to keep in touch and to know their respective locations precisely.

00:52:46.559 --> 00:52:48.221
Water conducts sound very well,

00:52:49.141 --> 00:52:50.681
five times faster than air.

00:52:54.423 --> 00:52:57.344
Whales can hear each other for hundreds of kilometers.

00:53:01.605 --> 00:53:03.066
The dialogue can break down.

00:53:23.514 --> 00:53:25.735
This danger is made of steel.

00:53:27.456 --> 00:53:31.699
It travels at 40 kilometers an hour and weighs thousands of tons.

00:53:36.501 --> 00:53:37.902
If the calf collides with it,

00:53:38.501 --> 00:53:39.563
it's all over for him.

00:54:23.423 --> 00:54:29.367
Revset Network software helps alert other vessels to the presence of a well and limit collisions.

00:54:44.132 --> 00:54:46.032
The Mediterranean represents 1%

00:54:46.333 --> 00:54:47.554
of the ocean surface.

00:54:48.374 --> 00:54:48.814
However,

00:54:49.275 --> 00:54:50.454
it is crossed by 30%

00:54:50.855 --> 00:54:52.195
of global maritime traffic.

00:54:55.258 --> 00:55:00.000
Thousands of boats navigated to reach the Suez Canal and avoid sailing around Africa.

00:55:01.581 --> 00:55:03.342
40 whales are killed every year,

00:55:04.143 --> 00:55:09.308
but a new program developed by the WWF and Quiet Ocean is raising hope.

00:55:16.295 --> 00:55:17.795
Using micro submarines,

00:55:18.137 --> 00:55:20.739
the Stop Collision System detects whale songs,

00:55:21.340 --> 00:55:22.721
locates them in real time,

00:55:23.061 --> 00:55:25.262
and transmits their position to every boat.

00:55:28.859 --> 00:55:29.860
Little Finn is safe,

00:55:30.380 --> 00:55:31.982
but he still hasn't eaten anything.

00:55:40.328 --> 00:55:42.710
His mother must teach him to feed on his own.

00:55:43.911 --> 00:55:44.712
So she listens.

00:55:46.835 --> 00:55:47.774
And here's the others.

00:56:13.119 --> 00:56:13.701
In spring,

00:56:14.001 --> 00:56:21.708
they travel up from the coast of North Africa towards the Gulf of Line for the abundant plankton and the promise of extraordinary feasts.

00:56:50.309 --> 00:56:51.710
Little Finn follows his mother.

00:56:54.653 --> 00:56:57.255
He observes her and imitates her gestures.

00:57:49.624 --> 00:57:49.905
Little

00:57:49.965 --> 00:57:52.286
Finn has just had his first meal on his own.

00:57:57.589 --> 00:57:59.150
And he thinks that's all there is to it.

00:57:59.890 --> 00:58:02.092
That he's all grown up and can now live on his own.

00:58:05.903 --> 00:58:06.664
Not quite yet.

00:58:08.286 --> 00:58:11.228
The day he learns to fish at a depth of 200 meters,

00:58:12.289 --> 00:58:13.710
Little Finn will be a real whale.

00:58:15.051 --> 00:58:16.251
And his mother will let him go.

00:58:17.793 --> 00:58:18.653
But not before then.

00:58:29.242 --> 00:58:29.942
It's September,

00:58:30.363 --> 00:58:31.383
on the coast of Greece.

00:58:36.000 --> 00:58:39.363
In the exact spot where Turtle laid her eggs eight weeks ago.

00:58:54.115 --> 00:58:54.576
Tonight,

00:58:55.117 --> 00:58:56.758
a great adventure begins.

00:59:00.981 --> 00:59:02.643
A baby loggerhead turtle.

00:59:04.739 --> 00:59:06.580
He must reach the sea before dawn.

00:59:08.340 --> 00:59:12.681
He must climb dozens of dunes and cross a desert without being spotted.

00:59:26.326 --> 00:59:27.586
In this perilous journey,

00:59:28.146 --> 00:59:30.887
the lives of thousands of young turtles are at stake.

00:59:47.427 --> 00:59:51.130
It's a full moon and it's guiding the baby turtles to safety.

00:59:53.751 --> 00:59:54.652
To head for the sea,

00:59:55.192 --> 00:59:57.815
he follows the reflection of the moon on the water.

01:00:05.547 --> 01:00:08.969
But other light sources attract him in the wrong direction.

01:00:16.911 --> 01:00:18.871
The baby is disoriented.

01:00:28.134 --> 01:00:30.076
He's heading right towards danger.

01:00:36.192 --> 01:00:42.677
They have been surveying this beach for months and have located all the turtle nests.

01:00:46.461 --> 01:00:48.983
Their mission tonight is to protect the babies.

01:00:58.691 --> 01:01:00.311
After two months of incubation,

01:01:00.791 --> 01:01:03.715
they come out at night when the temperature is low.

01:01:14.849 --> 01:01:17.311
This cage stops them from wandering off course.

01:01:22.354 --> 01:01:24.115
They help them find their way to the sea.

01:01:26.036 --> 01:01:32.278
But it is essential that they do the last few meters to the water themselves to train the muscles in their fins.

01:01:47.389 --> 01:01:49.891
But some hatching has escaped their attention.

01:01:52.032 --> 01:01:53.693
The first one was just the scout.

01:01:54.434 --> 01:01:57.175
His brothers and sisters are following just behind.

01:01:58.657 --> 01:02:01.059
They are all falling into the same trap.

01:02:15.105 --> 01:02:17.066
Because of artificial light sources,

01:02:17.726 --> 01:02:21.686
many little ones end up getting eaten or dried out by the sun.

01:02:28.289 --> 01:02:28.648
Luckily,

01:02:29.289 --> 01:02:30.250
they leave tracks.

01:02:31.970 --> 01:02:32.911
Kira,

01:02:34.151 --> 01:02:35.552
we've gone to the back of the beach.

01:02:50.809 --> 01:02:53.191
Do you want to?

01:02:53.251 --> 01:02:53.492
Yeah,

01:02:53.492 --> 01:02:54.452
I'll take one.

01:02:54.633 --> 01:02:56.755
I've got two quads on this back there.

01:02:57.315 --> 01:02:58.836
You're on time now.

01:02:59.497 --> 01:03:02.099
Yeah.

01:03:17.355 --> 01:03:21.399
These babies are now memorizing this exact point on earth.

01:03:24.042 --> 01:03:25.283
In 25 years,

01:03:25.723 --> 01:03:28.786
they will be able to return to this exact spot on this beach.

01:03:39.978 --> 01:03:41.519
On their quest to become adults.

01:03:42.135 --> 01:03:47.358
The young of the Mediterranean have had to surpass their limits and travel vast distances.

01:03:52.202 --> 01:03:53.603
They are the new generation.

01:03:57.545 --> 01:03:58.065
Meanwhile,

01:03:58.786 --> 01:03:59.505
others have grown.

01:04:01.146 --> 01:04:02.887
Old age is now upon them.

01:04:13.715 --> 01:04:17.637
Off the coast of France lives a small pod of bottlenose dolphins.

01:04:22.659 --> 01:04:25.199
A family headed by a very old female.

01:04:29.601 --> 01:04:30.900
She is their matriarch.

01:04:34.041 --> 01:04:36.802
Around her are her daughters and their little ones.

01:04:39.255 --> 01:04:42.159
Four generations of females all linked together.

01:04:46.804 --> 01:04:47.945
The matriarch is in her

01:04:48.467 --> 01:04:50.808
60s and her strength is starting to wane.

01:04:53.211 --> 01:04:54.313
Her muscles are stiffer,

01:04:55.454 --> 01:04:56.895
her joints less flexible,

01:04:59.139 --> 01:04:59.699
her sight...

01:05:00.307 --> 01:05:03.869
Her hearing or her senses are diminishing day by day.

01:05:14.472 --> 01:05:17.613
The matriarch guides her family across a vast territory,

01:05:18.094 --> 01:05:20.653
stretching from the French Riviera to the Camargue.

01:05:22.474 --> 01:05:23.635
But for the last few days,

01:05:23.954 --> 01:05:25.776
her navigation has been uncertain.

01:05:29.655 --> 01:05:31.577
