01:19:44.385 --> 01:19:46.026
How does the sea handle all this?

01:19:49.188 --> 01:19:52.010
What impact do these attacks have on her habitats?

01:19:54.533 --> 01:19:55.935
And how does she defend herself?

01:19:57.657 --> 01:19:59.920
There is a wonderful story that has a story.

01:20:08.606 --> 01:20:11.147
It happened here in the Gulf of Genoa

01:20:12.027 --> 01:20:12.787
30 years ago.

01:20:19.371 --> 01:20:20.710
Guillaume Neri was very young.

01:20:24.280 --> 01:20:26.543
He was not the world free diving champion yet,

01:20:27.023 --> 01:20:29.306
but his heart already belonged to the Mediterranean.

01:20:35.052 --> 01:20:37.454
This bay was a very rich natural habitat,

01:20:38.056 --> 01:20:40.679
until one of the greatest ever disasters struck.

01:20:44.076 --> 01:20:46.337
On the 11th of April 1991,

01:20:46.679 --> 01:20:51.222
the supertanker Amoco Milford Haven exploded two kilometers off the coast.

01:20:57.489 --> 01:21:01.492
10 000 tons of oil sank and were deposited 80 meters down.

01:21:15.555 --> 01:21:19.577
The haven left a deadly slick drifting towards the Italian and French coasts.

01:21:35.465 --> 01:21:35.585
It

01:21:35.586 --> 01:21:40.167
is the most serious ecological disaster ever recorded in the Mediterranean.

01:21:54.240 --> 01:21:55.820
All this life damaged by oil.

01:22:02.302 --> 01:22:03.302
30 years later,

01:22:03.963 --> 01:22:05.944
Guillaume returns to the scene of the disaster.

01:22:15.686 --> 01:22:17.587
How did the sea overcome this ordeal?

01:22:21.931 --> 01:22:23.733
What became of the steel monster?

01:22:29.255 --> 01:22:31.956
The haven is still there on the bottom

01:22:37.358 --> 01:22:46.943
334 meters long an Eiffel Tower lying on its side the biggest wreck in the world

01:23:01.811 --> 01:23:03.233
Are there any signs of life?

